{"call_id": "6a1f80c619b34ec582b11e17744dbe77", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/fad/PATENTS/query1/full-01/results/6a1f80c619b34ec582b11e17744dbe77.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"G06F\\n\\nMethodology: Patent filings were counted per year (filing year extracted from filing_date) for each CPC technology area rolled up to level 5 (subclass) of the CPC hierarchy, as defined in the CPCDefinition_database (level = 5, e.g., G06F). Each patent was counted once per distinct subclass. An exponential moving average of yearly filing counts was computed per subclass with smoothing factor alpha = 0.2 (EMA_t = 0.2 * count_t + 0.8 * EMA_{t-1}, over a complete zero-filled year grid 1877-2024; results verified robust to EMA initialization variants). For each year, the level-5 CPC area with the highest EMA was identified; the area whose best (top-EMA) year is 2022 is G06F (Electric digital data processing), with EMA_2022 = 1106.5, ahead of Y02E (868.1) and Y02P (634.6).\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
